# Notes

This module exists to keep `AGENTS.md` honest.

It was written using nothing but that guide — no reference, no other example —
and it touches every construct the guide teaches: an enum, an aggregate with an
invariant and an operation, a command, an event, a checked error, a projected
dto, a query, both directions of port, a service, three endpoints, the
infrastructure block and three scenarios.

CI checks it, runs its scenarios and compiles it to every target. So if the
guide ever describes syntax the compiler no longer accepts, this file fails
before anyone is misled by it.

## enum NoteState
- Draft
- Published

## aggregate Note
identified by id

- id: uuid, required
- title: text, required, min length 1, max length 200
- body: text, optional
- state: NoteState, required, default Draft
- createdAt: timestamp, required
- publishedAt: timestamp, optional

invariant "a published note has a timestamp":
  state is not Published or publishedAt is present

operation publish (at: timestamp) -> nothing:
  set state to Published
  set publishedAt to at

## command CreateNote
- title: text, required, min length 1
- body: text, optional

## event NotePublished from Note
topic note-published

- noteId: uuid, required
- publishedAt: timestamp, required

## error NoteNotFound (checked, status 404)
message: "no note exists with id {noteId}"

- noteId: uuid, required

## dto NoteSummary projects Note
- id: uuid, required
- title: text, required
- state: NoteState, required

## query NoteSearch over Note

- state: NoteState, optional
- titleContains: text, optional

match note.state is state
match note.title contains titleContains

sort by note.createdAt descending
limit 50

## port NoteRepository (outbound)
using in-memory

- find note by id (id: uuid) -> Note or NoteNotFound
- search notes (criteria: NoteSearch) -> list of Note
- save note (note: Note) -> nothing

## port NoteUseCases (inbound)

- create note (command: CreateNote) -> Note
- summarise note (id: uuid) -> NoteSummary or NoteNotFound
- publish note (id: uuid) -> NotePublished or NoteNotFound
- find notes (criteria: NoteSearch) -> list of Note

## service NoteService
uses NoteRepository
implements NoteUseCases

Every operation either does its job or says exactly why it could not.

operation create note (command: CreateNote) -> Note:
  let note be a new Note with id = new id, title = command.title, body = command.body, createdAt = now
  perform save note with note = note
  return note

operation summarise note (id: uuid) -> NoteSummary or NoteNotFound:
  let note be find note by id with id = id
  return NoteSummary from note

operation publish note (id: uuid) -> NotePublished or NoteNotFound:
  let note be find note by id with id = id
  let at be now
  set note.publishedAt to at
  set note.state to Published
  perform save note with note = note
  publish NotePublished with noteId = note.id, publishedAt = at
  return NotePublished with noteId = note.id, publishedAt = at

operation find notes (criteria: NoteSearch) -> list of Note:
  return search notes with criteria = criteria

## endpoint POST /notes
handled by NoteService.create note
request CreateNote
responds 201 with Note

## endpoint GET /notes/{id}
handled by NoteService.summarise note
responds 200 with NoteSummary
responds 404 when NoteNotFound

## endpoint POST /notes/{id}/publish
handled by NoteService.publish note
responds 200 with NotePublished
responds 404 when NoteNotFound

## infrastructure
port 8080
database notesdb using postgres version 16
deploy to docker

## scenario creating a note starts it as a draft

when created be create note with command = CreateNote with title = "First", body = nothing
then created.title is "First"
and created.state is Draft

## scenario publishing a note announces it

given note be Note with id = "n-1", title = "First", createdAt = now
when published be publish note with id = "n-1"
then published.noteId is "n-1"
and it publishes NotePublished

## scenario publishing one that is not there

given note be Note with id = "n-1", title = "First", createdAt = now
when publish note with id = "n-2"
then it fails with NoteNotFound
